# pcsplay.ps2 - a ball launched and the flippers worked.
#
# ⭐ THE MOUSE BUTTONS ARE THE TRIGGERS (pcsgame.inc): holding the left button
# pulls the plunger (full in about a second) and letting go is the shot, and
# the same button works the left flipper; the right button works the right
# flipper.  That is the Atari's own mapping - RUN.s:217 reads
# BUTN0 for the launch and FLIPRUN reads it for the flipper - not an invention.
#
# ⚠ `down`/`up` and not `click`: a flipper is LEVEL-sensitive (RUN.s:243, one
# frame per call, no edge), so a click that is three passes long flips once and
# drops.  Holding is the gesture the game is built round.
origin 320 240
gap 120

at 2.000    move to 160 440
+1.000      down left           # pull - a second held is a full spring
+1.200      up left             # ... and let go: LAUNCHHIT reads PDL0 >> 2
+2.000      down left           # left flipper
+0.300      up left
+0.400      down right          # right flipper
+0.300      up right
+1.000      down left
+0.300      up left
+0.600      down right
+0.300      up right
+1.000      down left
+0.300      up left
+2.000      down right
+0.300      up right
